Two years ago: COGS was 42% of revenue, beans 25% of that, so beans were about 10.5% of revenue. Other inputs were roughly 31.5% of revenue.

Today COGS is 58% of revenue. If beans alone drove the entire 16-point increase, beans would have to be 10.5 + 16 = 26.5% of revenue, which is about 46% of today's COGS. That's a massive shift — bean cost per cup would have to roughly 2.5x, holding volume constant.

